config BR2_PACKAGE_PLEXOS_NVIDIA
	bool "plexos-nvidia (open kernel modules)"
	depends on BR2_x86_64
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	help
	  NVIDIA's open GPU kernel modules, built from source against the
	  kernel this image ships (ADR-0015 step 3).

	  Turing and later only. Blackwell -- an RTX 5060 among them --
	  requires the open modules rather than the proprietary ones, which
	  is the reason this is the variant worth carrying rather than a
	  compromise.

	  This builds the kernel side alone: nvidia, nvidia-modeset,
	  nvidia-uvm, nvidia-drm and nvidia-peermem. It is not enough on its
	  own to transcode. Two things are still missing and each is its own
	  step:

	    - GSP firmware, which the driver requests at runtime as
	      nvidia/<version>/gsp_ga10x.bin and is not in this source
	      tarball (ADR-0015 step 4).
	    - The proprietary userspace, which is what Plex reaches NVDEC
	      and NVENC through (ADR-0015 step 5 onwards, and the step that
	      meets the project's unchosen licence).

	  Prefixed `plexos-` deliberately: a package directory name becomes
	  its kconfig symbol, and Buildroot already has an `nvidia-driver`
	  package pinned at 390.151. Colliding with it would have kconfig
	  merge the two definitions silently, which is a trap this project
	  has already recorded once.

	  Requires CONFIG_MODULES=y, which was set to `n` for the whole life
	  of this project until ADR-0015 reversed it.

comment "plexos-nvidia needs a kernel with loadable module support"
	depends on BR2_x86_64
	depends on !BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
